1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,781
This video shows you how to give a teammate their own account,

2
00:00:05,781 --> 00:00:08,070
with only the access they need.

3
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,986
In Admin, open Accounts, then Roles.

4
00:00:10,986 --> 00:00:14,771
The administrator role holds everything.

5
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:19,706
Add a role for the people who build pipelines.

6
00:00:19,706 --> 00:00:21,829
Call it pipeline-team.

7
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:29,381
A role gives each area a level: the shared configuration, or a worker group.

8
00:00:29,381 --> 00:00:30,750
A viewer reads it.

9
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:33,717
An editor also saves to it on a branch.

10
00:00:33,717 --> 00:00:36,710
A deployer also approves and deploys.

11
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:41,370
For example, an analyst who reviews how data is transformed is a viewer.

12
00:00:41,370 --> 00:00:44,124
The people who build pipelines are editors.

13
00:00:44,124 --> 00:00:48,630
The team lead who approves and deploys their changes is a deployer.

14
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:52,500
Your pipeline is in shared, and it runs on standalone.

15
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,950
Make the role an editor in both.

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,579
Save it.

17
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,832
Now add your teammate's account.

18
00:01:00,832 --> 00:01:03,830
On the Accounts tab, choose Add account.

19
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:06,357
Sam signs in with a password.

20
00:01:06,357 --> 00:01:11,670
Enter a display name and a username, and tick pipeline-team.

21
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,239
Add it.

22
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:16,691
smeltr shows Sam's one-time password, and only once.

23
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:22,556
Hand it to Sam over a channel you trust, then choose Done.

24
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:28,658
Here's Sam, in a browser of their own, signing in with that password.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,610
Before anything else, Sam chooses a password of their own.

26
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:39,055
Then Sam signs in with it.

27
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:45,076
Sam's menu has no Admin.

28
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:54,590
In Build, the pen on shared configuration says Sam can edit it, on a branch.

29
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,477
Check on learning.

30
00:01:56,677 --> 00:02:00,076
Sam builds pipelines but shouldn't deploy them.

31
00:02:00,076 --> 00:02:03,062
Which level does Sam's role give?

32
00:02:07,462 --> 00:02:08,021
Editor.

33
00:02:08,021 --> 00:02:10,259
An editor saves on a branch.

34
00:02:10,259 --> 00:02:14,135
Approving and deploying takes a deployer.

35
00:02:15,035 --> 00:02:19,049
Next, Sam makes a change, and you review it.
